From 0197c28aed78d4581da63b95269b011daa199635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: servediff <servediff@example.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:48:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] 0.4.97: --json counts must not move when only the flag moves

`compared_both_sides` counted every one-sided row whenever `--skip-absent` was absent, so
the same pair reported differences/both/hidden as 27/27/0 and 27/0/27. The field answers
"did anything change on the same code path", and a table of <absent> rows answered it the
same as a real comparison.

Now: differences = compared_both_sides + hidden_absent, always; the flag only shortens the
rows array. Text output no longer claims rows were skipped when they were not.

Regression test asserts equal counts across both modes and equality to the changed-row
count; checked over 60 random fixture pairs in both modes with 0 violations.
